# EVOLUTION - the third lane. Nightly, and it lands as a PR, never a direct commit.
# The promotion gate in RITUALS.md applies: the agent proposes, the founder taps.
#
# Same format as cron/watch.jobs and cron/work.jobs: one JSON job per line. It was
# written in crontab format ("0 3 * * *  work  <prose>") from the day it was added,
# so bin/install-cron.py died on line 5 with "is not valid JSON - Extra data: line 1
# column 3 (char 2)" -- json.loads reads the leading 0 as a number and then hits the
# space. The lane is ON in estate.yaml and the feature gate returns before load(),
# so the gate never hid it: every boot printed the error and installed nothing.
# Measured on the cluster in oke-check run 33355125388, pod hermes-agent-gateway-7cbdfdc7b5.
#
#   bin/install-cron.py cron/evolution.jobs --feature evolution
#
# No "skills" key on either job: skills/ carries no evolve-skill or curator skill,
# and `hermes cron create --skill <missing>` would fail at create time and leave the
# lane half-installed. The prompts name the work; add the skills when they exist.
{"name": "evolution-skills", "schedule": "0 3 * * *", "deliver": "telegram", "prompt": "Take the three most-used skills from the last 7 days. For each, run evolve_skill against the transcripts where it was used. Write the improved SKILL.md on a branch and open a PR titled \"evolution: <skill>\". Never commit to main. Append the run cost to logs/cost/evolution.txt."}
{"name": "evolution-curator", "schedule": "0 4 * * 0", "deliver": "telegram", "prompt": "Run the curator over the week's sessions. Write logs/curator/REPORT.md. Do not act on it - the report is for the Sunday review."}
